{
  "id": "bug-hotel-observer",
  "art": { "w": 1600, "h": 1200 },

  "_note": [
    "Canonical data for Bug Hotel Observer. game-design.md §6 is the schema",
    "contract; nothing here changes shape without editing that section too.",
    "Every path is relative and lowercase (CLAUDE.md rule). All geometry is in",
    "ART px against art.w x art.h and is mapped by shared/js/hotspot-scene.js's",
    "single cover-fit transform.",
    "P6 AUTHORED EVERY NUMBER BELOW AGAINST THE REAL 1600x1200 PLATES, read at",
    "full size with a 100 px coordinate grid laid over them. exteriorHotspot",
    "rects are the four compartments of assets/bg-hotel.jpg; zone centres are",
    "the arched hollows / tube mouths of the four interiors; the lens frame",
    "numbers are MEASURED from assets/props/magnifier.webp by",
    "tools/fix-cutouts.py's glass_aperture() and must be re-measured if that",
    "sprite is ever regenerated."
  ],

  "modes": [
    {
      "id": "bug-hunt",
      "title": "Bug Hunt",
      "intro": "mode-bug-hunt",
      "prompt": "find",
      "showsTargetPlaque": true,
      "wrongTapRepeatsPrompt": false,
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "id": "bug-detective",
      "title": "Bug Detective",
      "intro": "mode-bug-detective",
      "prompt": "clue",
      "showsTargetPlaque": false,
      "wrongTapRepeatsPrompt": true,
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "id": "my-bug-book",
      "title": "My Bug Book",
      "intro": "mode-my-bug-book",
      "prompt": "none",
      "showsTargetPlaque": false,
      "wrongTapRepeatsPrompt": false,
      "default": false,
      "review": true
    }
  ],

  "_lensNotes": [
    "frame.scale = 900 / 372 and frame.anchor = (366/900, 396/900): the glass",
    "hole of magnifier.webp is a circle of radius 186 px centred on (366, 396)",
    "of a 900x900 sprite. With these two numbers the module draws the frame so",
    "the authored hole lands EXACTLY on the clip circle — the ring's opaque",
    "inner edge and the edge of the magnified world are the same pixel.",
    "gripOffset/gripDir put the invisible drag button on the HANDLE (the",
    "handle leaves the ring at 0.768, 0.641 of a unit vector). At gripOffset",
    "205 with gripSize 0.62 the button never contains the glass CENTRE, so a",
    "bug that has just been revealed under the glass is still tappable, and",
    "the child's finger rests beside the glass instead of on top of it.",
    "startArt parks the glass in the one place that is >295 ART px (glass",
    "radius + half a bug) from EVERY zone of EVERY room, so no bug is ever",
    "half-visible inside the glass before the search begins."
  ],

  "lens": {
    "zoom": 1.6,
    "glassD": 360,
    "dwellMs": 600,
    "dwellRadiusArt": 150,
    "gripOffset": 205,
    "gripDir": { "x": 0.768, "y": 0.641 },
    "gripSize": 0.62,
    "gripMinCssPx": 140,
    "sprite": "assets/props/magnifier.webp",
    "frame": { "scale": 2.4194, "anchor": { "x": 0.4067, "y": 0.44 } },
    "startArt": { "x": 860, "y": 330 },
    "glintMs": 900
  },

  "_zoneNotes": [
    "Four authored nooks per room; exactly three carry a bug in any given round,",
    "chosen by a seeded FNV-1a draw so the empty nook moves between rounds.",
    "Every centre sits inside the portrait-safe band x in [420, 1180] and the",
    "HUD-clear band y in [300, 1000] (see game-design.md §4.4 keep-out table).",
    "A zone centre is where the bug's sprite box is CENTRED; the sprite is drawn",
    "at bugs[].artSize on its longest edge.",
    "P6: leaf, bark and log share one shadowbox composition (one arch top-left,",
    "three along the lower shelf), so they share one zone table read off the",
    "plates; bamboo is a different build and has its own four tube mouths. Every",
    "pair of centres in a room is >= 290 ART px apart, comfortably past the 150",
    "px dwell radius, so the glass can never be inside two nooks at once.",
    "The right-hand nooks sit at x ~1150 rather than dead centre in their arch",
    "(~1196): PORTRAIT only shows art x in [381, 1219], and a bug centred in the",
    "arch lost a quarter of itself off the right edge of an upright iPad."
  ],

